### 3.1 How the 32 RUN_OK breaks down

- 13 from RUN_NONZERO via Int+Float+String (x86_add3, x86_int_add/sub/mul/div/rem, x86_negint, x86_negzero, x86_paren_mul, x86_float, x86_hi_bind, x86_idid, x86_nstrcat)
- 1 from RUN_NONZERO via the new Loop fast path (x86_for)
- 7 from REFUSED via If (x86_ident_if, x86_if_add, x86_int_gt/lt/gte/lte/neq)
- 1 from REFUSED via String alias (x86_alias)
- 1 from ASM_FAIL via If (x86_elseif)
- 9 from REFUSED via Call (x86_5th, x86_6th, x86_fth, x86_snd, x86_id_call, x86_greet_call, x86_call, x86_cat, x86_buf_ovf)
- = **32 RUN_OK**

### 3.2 The 3 RUN_NONZERO that stay (blocked by LLVM lane)

- x86_for: now RUN_OK (Loop fast path covers it). 0 left.
- x86_heap_alloc, x86_heap_free: missing runtime functions (`heap_alloc_test`, `oo_alloc`, `oo_write_int`, `oo_read_int`, `oo_free` are not defined anywhere in the source tree). These need a runtime-side addition. Out of lane.

### 3.3 The 13 REFUSED that stay (genuine EXPECT_REFUSE)

- challenge_math_solvers, challenge_math_accuracy, llvm_generic_adt_smoke, prove_prod_complex, prove_prod_eigen, adv_err_res_list_struct, result_option_ok_some, test_csv_streaming, hop_probe, actor_path_a, adv_result_list_arc_asan, adv_result_list_struct_basic, list_struct_smoke, list_string — all EXPECT_REFUSE. They use features the x86 lane cannot lower: complex math, list_struct, dynamic dispatch. LLVM lane work.

### 3.4 The 2 ASM_FAIL that stay (blocked by LLVM lane)

- x86_fib: recursive function call. Needs real call/ret emission with register spilling. LLVM lane work.
- list_struct_smoke: struct field access. Needs struct lowering. LLVM lane work.

