## 10. Risks and caveats

- The 7th C1 measurement cannot be run until the next oodac binary build. The build queue has been contention-bound with parallel agents.
- The x86_ssa_emit_loop.oo fast path has not been tested end-to-end. The C1 smoke can only verify the type-checker (`ooda check`) and grep-assertions (lock smoke), not the actual runtime output. A full validation requires a binary build.
- The 32 RUN_OK prediction assumes the existing 13 fast-path commits land in the binary alongside the 2 new commits. If the build picks up only the 2 new commits, the predicted 7th is much lower (only the +1 from x86_for, plus the multi-println guard which doesn't add any C1 movement).
